
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUILD OUTPUT — never tracked.
# Measured 2026-08-01, before the first public push: 1,816 tracked files and
# 1.6 GB of compiler output (149 .rlib, 512 .o, 149 .rmeta, a 90 MB .pdb) had
# been committed alongside the source, against 32.5 MB of actual project. That
# is not a repository, it is a build directory with a repository inside it --
# and GitHub rejects any push over 2 GB, so it could not have been published
# at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
rust/*/target-netstack/
rust/*/target/
build/
.gradle/
.avd-guard/

# Backups taken before a risky edit (*.pre-<reason>.bak). Useful locally,
# meaningless to anyone else, and they double the weight of every binary.
*.bak

# The Rust engine and UI shared objects are BUILD OUTPUT (64 MB each, over
# GitHub's 50 MB warning threshold). Build them with the cargo-ndk command in
# README.md -- shipping them in git would make every clone pay for a binary
# that must be rebuilt from source anyway.
libumdnscrypt/src/main/jniLibs/*/*.so

# Local run artifacts
hosts_probe.txt
*.png.tmp
